{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Until a loaf of bread</b> — He loses his wealth, until he needs to borrow a loaf of bread from people." "<b>And another man's wife</b> — She hunts the soul of the one who commits adultery with her. And he said: <b>precious</b> — because it is drawn from the light of HaShem. <b>She hunts</b> — for she hunts, like the expression תצודנה (they hunt) souls."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:14.158622938Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}